---
import LegalLayout from '@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site, fullAddress } from '@/config/site';
import { pages } from '@/data/pages';

const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'Terms and conditions', path: '/terms' },
];
---

<LegalLayout {...pages.terms} heading="Terms and conditions" updated="2026-10-13" crumbs={crumbs}>
  <p>
    These terms govern your use of the {site.legalName} website. By using the site you agree to them. They do not govern client engagements,
    which are covered by a separate services agreement.
  </p>

  <h2>Use of the website</h2>
  <p>You may use this website to learn about our services and to contact us. You agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>use the site in any way that breaks the law or infringes anyone’s rights;</li>
    <li>attempt to gain unauthorised access to the site, its servers or connected systems;</li>
    <li>send spam, malware or automated submissions through our forms;</li>
    <li>scrape or copy the site’s content at scale without our written permission.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Content and intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    The text, design, graphics, illustrations and code on this site belong to {site.legalName} or its licensors and are protected by copyright and
    trademark law. You may share links to our pages and quote short extracts with attribution. Any other use needs our written permission.
  </p>

  <h2>Information on the site</h2>
  <p>
    We work to keep the information on this site accurate and current, but it is general information, not professional, legal, tax or financial
    advice. Prices shown are starting points; a binding price is agreed in writing after discovery. Engagement blueprints describe how we typically
    run engagements and are not guarantees of specific results.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party links and services</h2>
  <p>
    The site links to and embeds third-party services such as Calendly, Google Maps and LinkedIn. We are not responsible for their content or
    privacy practices; your use of them is governed by their own terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    The website is provided “as is”. To the fullest extent the law allows, {site.legalName} is not liable for any indirect or consequential loss
    arising from your use of the site, or for interruptions or errors. Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law.
  </p>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>How we handle personal information is explained in our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Delaware, and the courts of Delaware have jurisdiction over any dispute about them.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update these terms from time to time. The date at the top of this page shows when they last changed.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>{site.legalName}, {fullAddress}. <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>, {site.phone}.</p>
</LegalLayout>
